WEBVTT

00:02.640 --> 00:04.310
SIGN: NANKATSU SC - MUSASHI FC

00:04.310 --> 00:07.150
All right, it's our turn now!

00:07.150 --> 00:09.580
And right after Meiwa and Furano's fierce match.

00:09.580 --> 00:11.580
Let's liven up the mood!

00:11.580 --> 00:12.610
Yeah!

00:13.650 --> 00:15.820
<i>It's time for the second match of the semi-finals,</i>

00:15.820 --> 00:17.990
<i>Nankatsu SC vs. Musashi FC.</i>

00:17.990 --> 00:21.740
<i>Both teams' players have just entered the field.</i>

00:24.080 --> 00:25.120
Misugi!

00:25.120 --> 00:26.710
Look over here!

00:26.710 --> 00:29.340
Good luck, Misugi!

00:29.340 --> 00:32.840
Hooray! Hooray! Nankatsu!

00:32.840 --> 00:36.010
Fight! Fight! Nankatsu!

00:36.500 --> 00:40.300
<i>The most heavily anticipated match of this tournament</i>

00:40.300 --> 00:42.340
<i>is finally about to begin.</i>

00:42.340 --> 00:44.060
<i>Let's do this, Tsubasa.</i>

00:45.140 --> 00:48.350
<i>I won't lose, Misugi.</i>

01:06.100 --> 01:11.730
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:06.150 --> 01:11.780
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:11.730 --> 01:16.740
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:11.780 --> 01:16.740
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:17.410 --> 01:22.580
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:17.410 --> 01:22.620
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:23.290 --> 01:30.910
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:23.290 --> 01:30.910
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:30.910 --> 01:36.680
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:30.910 --> 01:36.720
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:36.680 --> 01:45.180
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:36.720 --> 01:45.180
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:45.180 --> 01:50.970
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:45.180 --> 01:50.970
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:50.970 --> 01:56.900
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:50.970 --> 01:56.900
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:56.900 --> 01:58.410
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:58.410 --> 02:05.700
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:58.410 --> 02:05.700
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:05.700 --> 02:08.620
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:05.700 --> 02:08.620
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:08.620 --> 02:13.550
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

02:08.620 --> 02:13.550
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:24.180 --> 02:28.580
<b><b>EPISODE 20:
MUSASHI'S SECRET PLAN</b></b>

02:25.580 --> 02:28.790
<i>Both teams' players have dispersed across the field.</i>

02:30.940 --> 02:33.790
<i>Nankatsu vs. Musashi kicks off!</i>

02:35.960 --> 02:38.020
Marking you in midfield...

02:38.020 --> 02:39.170
...is up to us two!

02:40.550 --> 02:41.300
Wh—

02:41.300 --> 02:43.300
Sano! Send it to Honma!

02:43.300 --> 02:43.800
Okay.

02:47.860 --> 02:49.980
<i>A wing attack from Musashi!</i>

02:49.980 --> 02:50.980
I'll stop them.

02:53.570 --> 02:55.230
Like I'd let you!

02:55.230 --> 02:57.360
<i>Honma sends up a cross down the middle.</i>

02:57.360 --> 03:00.030
Hold on! We're in charge of marking you in front of the goal.

03:01.010 --> 03:02.370
Go, Sanada!

03:02.370 --> 03:03.360
Wh—

03:03.360 --> 03:05.250
<i>That was a nice move.</i>

03:05.250 --> 03:08.740
<i>Since Misugi is heavily marked, Sanada is completey unmarked.</i>

03:08.740 --> 03:10.500
What?!

03:10.500 --> 03:11.710
I got it!

03:13.730 --> 03:16.130
<i>Morisaki catches it firmly!</i>

03:16.130 --> 03:18.130
<i>The shot goes straight at the goalkeeper!</i>

03:18.130 --> 03:19.480
Damn it!

03:19.480 --> 03:22.090
<i>Musashi almost had that.</i>

03:22.090 --> 03:26.390
<i>When Misugi's on the field, there's a certain rhythm to their attacks.</i>

03:26.390 --> 03:29.980
<i>He has no unnecessary movements.</i>

03:29.980 --> 03:31.930
<i>That's Misugi for you.</i>

03:32.380 --> 03:33.100
Here!

03:35.020 --> 03:38.650
<i>Let's see what Musashi's capable of.</i>

03:40.070 --> 03:42.450
Go, Misaki!

03:47.490 --> 03:49.140
<i>This is different.</i>

03:49.140 --> 03:51.790
<i>They're keeping us in check more than the other teams.</i>

03:55.040 --> 03:58.790
Dribbling down the sideline is my specialty!

03:58.790 --> 04:01.650
Be careful! He'll send a cross in!

04:01.650 --> 04:02.920
Bring it on, Taki!

04:02.920 --> 04:04.050
Here!

04:04.050 --> 04:06.470
<i>He sends the ball in front of the goal to Kisugi—</i>

04:07.000 --> 04:08.470
<i>Wait, it was for Tsubasa!</i>

04:08.470 --> 04:11.220
<i>Nankatsu uses Kisugi as a decoy!</i>

04:11.220 --> 04:13.850
Let's go! I'm gonna shoot!

04:15.480 --> 04:17.290
<i>It's Misugi with a swift interception!</i>

04:17.290 --> 04:19.270
<i>Nankatsu won't be having the first goal!</i>

04:22.150 --> 04:24.070
It's on, Tsubasa!

04:24.070 --> 04:26.820
All right! I accept your challenge, Misugi!

04:26.820 --> 04:30.580
<i>This is Misugi and Tsubasa's first showdown.</i>

04:30.580 --> 04:32.290
<i>Nankatsu vs. Musashi!</i>

04:32.290 --> 04:33.790
<i>Here comes the first highlight of the match.</i>

04:33.790 --> 04:35.080
Tsubasa!

04:37.080 --> 04:38.070
This time...

04:38.070 --> 04:38.920
...we'll block your path!

04:39.470 --> 04:41.550
<i>They're coming at him from every direction.</i>

04:41.550 --> 04:43.670
<i>What will Misugi do?</i>

04:45.620 --> 04:47.300
<i>I'll break past them with a dribble!</i>

04:48.680 --> 04:50.970
<i>Misugi feints!</i>

04:50.970 --> 04:51.760
Good!

04:51.760 --> 04:54.140
<i>Tsubasa catches up with him!</i>

04:57.080 --> 05:00.060
<i>Misugi jumps and dodges!</i>

05:02.020 --> 05:04.110
<i>He shoots!</i>

05:05.810 --> 05:08.820
<i>The ball flies away!</i>

05:09.300 --> 05:12.200
<i>It looks like Tsubasa barely managed to deflect it away.</i>

05:12.200 --> 05:18.080
<i>Tsubasa did really well to endure Misugi's overwhelming attack.</i>

05:18.080 --> 05:20.260
<i>As expected of Tsubasa.</i>

05:20.260 --> 05:24.840
<i>It looks like I won't win unless I lay all my cards on the table.</i>

05:24.840 --> 05:27.810
<i>Misugi, you're really amazing.</i>

05:27.810 --> 05:30.850
<i>I can't wait to see all of your different techniques.</i>

05:34.480 --> 05:38.600
<i>Every second of this match will need my utmost focus.</i>

05:47.300 --> 05:48.360
Jun...

05:48.360 --> 05:51.030
What, you're here?

05:51.030 --> 05:53.030
Oh, you too?

05:53.030 --> 05:54.120
Well, yeah.

05:54.120 --> 05:58.580
Jun called and said that no matter what, he wanted me to come to today's match.

05:59.200 --> 06:01.420
Could it be, he—

06:07.540 --> 06:09.450
What's wrong, Roberto?

06:10.930 --> 06:14.180
Is there something troubling you about Tsubasa's play?

06:14.180 --> 06:16.310
No, far from it.

06:16.310 --> 06:23.270
Tsubasa is playing well. In fact, he's grown much more than I expected him to in this tournament.

06:23.270 --> 06:25.920
So, Tsubasa's sure to win this match too, right?

06:25.920 --> 06:26.650
Of course.

06:26.650 --> 06:30.650
There are many other skillful players in Japan, like Misugi.

06:30.650 --> 06:34.740
But, only Tsubasa can become the champion.

06:34.740 --> 06:38.660
And then you'll take Tsubasa to Brazil with you when he becomes the champion, Roberto.

06:45.170 --> 06:47.670
<i>I can't send a pass like this.</i>

06:47.670 --> 06:48.410
Misaki!

06:48.410 --> 06:49.260
Watch out!

06:50.470 --> 06:51.380
<i>Oh no!</i>

06:51.380 --> 06:54.140
<i>That's the Young Noble of the Field for you!</i>

06:55.890 --> 06:57.060
Ichinose!

06:57.060 --> 06:57.970
Got it!

07:02.060 --> 07:05.820
<i>That was close! The ball hit the post.</i>

07:09.320 --> 07:10.940
Don't let it get to you, Ichinose.

07:10.940 --> 07:11.570
Okay.

07:11.570 --> 07:13.220
Jun...

07:13.220 --> 07:15.570
Honey, there comes a time in the life of a man

07:15.570 --> 07:22.670
where he needs to do everything he can and push his limits in order to realize his goal.

07:24.030 --> 07:26.880
For Jun, this match is his moment.

07:26.880 --> 07:30.720
Let's stay, that all the pieces might fall in place for him today.

07:33.500 --> 07:35.680
<i>I can't just sit and wait for the ball to come to me.</i>

07:35.680 --> 07:36.680
<i>If that's the case...</i>

07:38.100 --> 07:43.100
<i>Misugi doesn't pass the ball and lies in wait for Tsubasa.</i>

07:43.100 --> 07:44.230
Tsubasa!

07:44.230 --> 07:47.190
<i>Does this show his confidence that he won't lose the ball?</i>

07:47.190 --> 07:52.860
<i>Tsubasa, I've been eagerly waiting to have this one-on-one showdown with you.</i>

07:52.860 --> 07:55.160
<i>I'll definitely take the ball from you!</i>

07:56.160 --> 07:58.910
<i>Tsubasa forcefully checks Misugi here.</i>

08:03.870 --> 08:05.030
Misugi!

08:05.030 --> 08:06.670
Tsubasa! We're attacking now!

08:08.670 --> 08:11.260
<i>This is a chance for Nankatsu!</i>

08:11.260 --> 08:12.840
<i>A pass for Tsubasa!</i>

08:15.000 --> 08:18.260
<i>He's a second too late!</i>

08:18.260 --> 08:19.260
Damn it!

08:19.260 --> 08:20.990
<i>What's wrong, Tsubasa?</i>

08:20.990 --> 08:22.930
<i>You were late on that run forward.</i>

08:22.930 --> 08:24.380
<i>Tsubasa...</i>

08:24.380 --> 08:27.650
<i>Could it be that you know, and are worried about my heart?</i>

08:28.730 --> 08:32.440
<i>If that's so... you're much too naive!</i>

08:32.440 --> 08:35.100
<i>I won't lose to a mere heart disease!</i>

08:35.100 --> 08:36.160
What?!

08:36.680 --> 08:39.830
<i>And Tsubasa, I won't lose to you either!</i>

08:42.200 --> 08:43.160
<i>Misugi...</i>

08:43.160 --> 08:45.870
I won't let you go any further!

08:45.870 --> 08:49.090
<i>Nankatsu goes to stop him with three players.</i>

08:51.920 --> 08:53.090
Take this!

08:53.090 --> 08:55.930
<i>It's a desperate double tackle from Nankatsu!</i>

08:57.260 --> 08:58.510
What?!

09:04.700 --> 09:07.900
<i>Goal! He scores with a fascinating mid-air move!</i>

09:09.090 --> 09:11.900
<i>That was an amazingly bold move!</i>

09:11.900 --> 09:13.560
<i>Jun Misugi!</i>

09:13.560 --> 09:15.840
<i>He really is the Young Noble of the Field!</i>

09:15.840 --> 09:17.530
C-cool...

09:17.530 --> 09:21.740
<i>In the 10th minute of the first half, Musashi finally leads by a goal.</i>

09:21.740 --> 09:24.250
Damn it, he was so quick.

09:24.250 --> 09:25.380
Damn it all!

09:25.380 --> 09:27.500
We couldn't do anything.

09:27.500 --> 09:29.660
Misugi is really amazing!

09:29.660 --> 09:30.250
Wha—

09:30.900 --> 09:33.700
However, football is played with 11 people.

09:33.700 --> 09:35.460
We haven't lost yet.

09:35.460 --> 09:38.800
You're right! There's still plenty of time.

09:38.800 --> 09:40.440
We'll quickly score a goal too.

09:40.440 --> 09:43.470
We'll tie the score in this first half, and even take the lead!

09:43.470 --> 09:45.220
Yeah!

09:48.280 --> 09:50.060
<i>The game resumes.</i>

09:50.060 --> 09:54.900
After conceding a goal, Nankatsu is sure to try and enable Tsubasa.

09:54.900 --> 09:58.900
Sano, Kido! You two are to completely mark Tsubasa.

09:58.900 --> 09:59.860
Yes!

10:02.000 --> 10:03.120
Misaki!

10:03.120 --> 10:04.990
<i>My opponents are here.</i>

10:04.990 --> 10:06.450
<i>I'll dribble past them!</i>

10:07.960 --> 10:09.670
What?

10:09.670 --> 10:13.210
<i>Nankatsu's Golden Duo closes in on the goal.</i>

10:13.210 --> 10:15.250
<i>It's going well. Tsubasa!</i>

10:15.250 --> 10:17.420
<i>The ball is sent directly to Tsubasa.</i>

10:17.420 --> 10:17.970
<i>All right!</i>

10:18.980 --> 10:20.720
<i>Misugi cuts the pass!</i>

10:20.720 --> 10:23.390
<i>Nankatsu's Golden Duo can't make their play!</i>

10:24.640 --> 10:26.850
<i>It's Musashi's counterattack!</i>

10:26.850 --> 10:27.900
Damn it!

10:27.900 --> 10:30.270
How long do they plan on underestimating us?!

10:31.640 --> 10:33.240
Izawa's right.

10:33.240 --> 10:36.330
Nankatsu's more than just Tsubasa and Misaki!

10:36.330 --> 10:36.980
Taki!

10:38.170 --> 10:38.940
<i>That's right!</i>

10:38.940 --> 10:42.450
<i>Nankatsu has 11 players after all!</i>

10:42.450 --> 10:43.410
Mark him!

10:43.410 --> 10:45.450
We're being dragged into their pace!

10:45.450 --> 10:46.580
Okay!

10:47.620 --> 10:49.370
Taki, over here!

10:49.370 --> 10:50.980
I'm counting on you, Misaki!

10:50.980 --> 10:54.340
<i>Nankatsu shows off perfect team play!</i>

10:54.340 --> 10:57.300
<i>It's no use, Tsubasa's being marked.</i>

10:57.800 --> 10:59.550
Kisugi, I'm leaving it to you!

11:00.260 --> 11:03.050
<i>Misugi, I won't let you have the ball.</i>

11:05.180 --> 11:08.180
<i>Kisugi diverts the ball to the left with his head.</i>

11:08.180 --> 11:10.430
<i>Tsubasa shakes off the defense!</i>

11:10.430 --> 11:12.020
<i>Score, Tsubasa!</i>

11:12.020 --> 11:13.690
<i>Everyone worked hard to create this chance!</i>

11:13.690 --> 11:15.900
<i>As the ace, it's your duty to score!</i>

11:15.900 --> 11:18.180
<i>If I try to trap the ball, it'll be too late.</i>

11:18.180 --> 11:21.200
<i>I'm Nankatsu's ace!</i>

11:22.010 --> 11:26.240
<i>Here it is! Tsubasa's specialty, the overhead kick!</i>

11:31.000 --> 11:32.480
<i>It's in!</i>

11:32.480 --> 11:35.750
<i>Against this marvelous feat, the goalkeeper couldn't even move an inch!</i>

11:35.750 --> 11:37.750
<i>The score is 1-1 and Nankatsu has caught up!</i>

11:38.110 --> 11:39.380
I did it!

11:39.380 --> 11:40.880
Amazing!

11:40.880 --> 11:42.760
That was great, Tsubasa!

11:42.760 --> 11:44.160
Tsubasa!

11:44.160 --> 11:45.760
You're great, Tsubasa!

11:46.320 --> 11:48.240
<i>As expected of you, Tsubasa.</i>

11:48.240 --> 11:50.770
<i>I have nothing more to say to you.</i>

11:52.500 --> 11:54.280
<i>Mom, dad...</i>

11:54.280 --> 11:55.270
<i>He's great, isn't he?</i>

11:55.270 --> 11:59.280
<i>That's Tsubasa, my final opponent in my very last match.</i>

12:00.350 --> 12:01.530
Jun...

12:01.530 --> 12:04.760
All right, guys! It's our turn now.

12:04.760 --> 12:07.880
Let's show them Musashi FC's true power!

12:07.880 --> 12:09.030
All right!

12:19.840 --> 12:22.260
<i>The flow of the match has focused near Nankatsu's goal.</i>

12:22.260 --> 12:24.510
<i>Will Musashi score again?</i>

12:24.510 --> 12:26.010
I won't let you go!

12:26.010 --> 12:26.760
Nakajima!

12:29.260 --> 12:32.430
<i>Unable to press on, he passes the ball to Misugi with a back pass.</i>

12:33.880 --> 12:37.180
<i>Oh, Tsubasa has come to challenge him!</i>

12:37.180 --> 12:40.150
<i>It's their second showdown!</i>

12:40.150 --> 12:44.200
Tsubasa, do you know about my heart?

12:44.200 --> 12:44.740
Huh?!

12:46.200 --> 12:49.120
<i>So you do know, Tsubasa.</i>

12:49.120 --> 12:51.790
<i>What happened to Tsubasa?</i>

12:52.700 --> 12:53.450
I'll clear the ball!

12:53.450 --> 12:54.540
Make it in this time!

12:55.420 --> 12:57.040
<i>The heading showdown is a tie!</i>

12:59.120 --> 12:59.850
All right!

12:59.850 --> 13:02.750
<i>Morisaki catches the ball tightly!</i>

13:02.750 --> 13:04.380
Misugi!

13:04.380 --> 13:07.240
Tsubasa, no matter what happens,

13:07.240 --> 13:08.720
don't you dare pull your punches.

13:09.920 --> 13:10.890
Of course!

13:12.770 --> 13:15.190
<i>The showdowns today are all tied up,</i>

13:15.190 --> 13:17.330
<i>just like the score.</i>

13:17.330 --> 13:20.020
<i>Which side will manage to score a second goal first?</i>

13:20.020 --> 13:23.810
All right. If Nankatsu starts following Tsubasa's pace,

13:23.810 --> 13:25.020
we'll use that strategy.

13:25.020 --> 13:25.780
Yes!

13:25.780 --> 13:28.070
Go! Nankatsu!

13:28.070 --> 13:28.740
All right!

13:28.740 --> 13:29.870
It's time to reverse the score!

13:34.380 --> 13:38.830
<i>Tsubasa is in front of the goal and clear of any markers!</i>

13:41.340 --> 13:42.460
Tsubasa!

13:42.460 --> 13:45.890
<i>Will Misaki's long pass reach him?</i>

13:45.890 --> 13:46.970
<i>The pass reaches him!</i>

13:46.970 --> 13:50.090
<i>Tsubasa has no markers in front of the goal!</i>

13:50.090 --> 13:52.560
Take that!

13:52.560 --> 13:54.420
<i>It's in!</i>

13:54.420 --> 13:55.250
All right!

13:55.250 --> 13:57.310
<i>Nankatsu reverses the score in no time!</i>

13:57.840 --> 13:59.810
<i>They are celebrating wildly!</i>

13:59.810 --> 14:01.220
Tsubasa!

14:01.220 --> 14:02.740
You did it!

14:05.610 --> 14:06.880
<i>What's this?</i>

14:06.880 --> 14:09.730
<i>Assistant referee has his flag raised!</i>

14:09.730 --> 14:11.500
<i>Tsubasa is ruled offside!</i>

14:11.500 --> 14:13.120
What? Offside?

14:15.060 --> 14:16.760
<i>Offside.</i>

14:16.760 --> 14:21.800
<i>It's when a player on the attacking side is sent a pass from a teammate while they're on the opponent's side,</i>

14:21.800 --> 14:27.740
<i>and there are less than two people to beat on the defense, goalkeeper included.</i>

14:27.740 --> 14:36.140
<i>Accordingly, the offside trap is a tactic that uses this rule, leaving a player alone in the offside position.</i>

14:36.140 --> 14:40.690
That's preposterous! Could Musashi truly have mastered the offside trap?!

14:42.550 --> 14:43.230
Taki!

14:44.150 --> 14:45.900
All right! This time!

14:46.340 --> 14:48.150
<i>Tsubasa is unmarked once more!</i>

14:51.110 --> 14:52.110
All right!

14:55.090 --> 14:57.760
<i>Offside again!</i>

14:57.760 --> 14:59.760
<i>This is the offside trap!</i>

14:59.760 --> 15:01.620
I was right!

15:01.620 --> 15:03.380
Damn it!

15:03.380 --> 15:06.250
<i>Tsubasa was prevented from shooting</i>

15:06.250 --> 15:08.260
<i>through repeated offside traps.</i>

15:12.640 --> 15:13.800
<i>Offside!</i>

15:13.800 --> 15:17.250
<i>Tsubasa has been locked out completely!</i>

15:17.250 --> 15:21.440
<i>Nankatsu's eleven look cornered by this turn of events!</i>

15:21.440 --> 15:24.090
Get forward while they're distracted!

15:24.090 --> 15:24.690
Let's go!

15:24.690 --> 15:26.060
Yeah!

15:26.060 --> 15:28.190
<i>Musashi rushes forward in a lightning-fast attack!</i>

15:28.190 --> 15:29.030
Honma!

15:29.990 --> 15:31.700
<i>The ball is sent to the right side!</i>

15:31.700 --> 15:34.200
<i>Sanada is running toward the goal!</i>

15:39.020 --> 15:41.080
The ball is my friend!

15:41.080 --> 15:44.420
I'm not scared of it! But it hurts all the same!

15:44.420 --> 15:46.670
All right! Third time's the charm!

15:47.980 --> 15:49.800
<i>Morisaki prevents the shot!</i>

15:49.800 --> 15:51.670
Damn it! Again!

15:53.150 --> 15:55.970
<i>Ah, the ball is coming towards Misugi!</i>

15:55.970 --> 15:56.890
Ah!

15:56.890 --> 15:59.480
<i>Tsubasa, let me show you that you're</i>

15:59.480 --> 16:02.440
<i>not the only one that can pull that shot off!</i>

16:06.540 --> 16:07.360
Ah! That's—

16:07.360 --> 16:09.580
<i>What is this?!</i>

16:09.580 --> 16:13.280
<i>Misugi perfectly executes his own overhead kick!</i>

16:17.640 --> 16:19.740
<i>It brilliantly pierces the back of the net!</i>

16:20.790 --> 16:23.440
<i>Musashi takes the lead once more!</i>

16:25.120 --> 16:27.320
<i>The match has completely fallen into Musashi's—</i>

16:27.320 --> 16:30.300
<i>No, it has fallen into Misugi's pace!</i>

16:31.000 --> 16:33.300
<i>And the whistle marks the end of the first half!</i>

16:33.300 --> 16:38.930
<i>The match is 2-1, with Musashi in the lead at the half!</i>

16:39.450 --> 16:41.310
H-he's strong!

16:42.010 --> 16:43.810
Good job, boys!

16:43.810 --> 16:46.370
Keep this pace in the second half too!

16:46.370 --> 16:47.310
Yes!

16:47.940 --> 16:49.520
Are you all right, Misugi?

16:49.520 --> 16:52.090
Yes, I can keep going in the second half, too.

16:52.090 --> 16:53.070
That's good to hear.

16:53.070 --> 16:55.070
Manager, can I have a word?

16:55.070 --> 16:57.070
Oh, sure!

16:57.070 --> 16:59.080
What's happened to you guys?

16:59.080 --> 17:01.390
You guys aren't as energetic as usual.

17:01.390 --> 17:06.320
Coach, Misugi's Musashi are a tough nut to crack.

17:06.320 --> 17:09.840
It feels like he has eyes on the back of his head.

17:09.840 --> 17:11.380
While it's probably true that he's the kind of prodigy

17:11.380 --> 17:14.800
that only appears every few years,

17:14.800 --> 17:17.340
football is a team sport through and through.

17:17.340 --> 17:20.680
Our teamwork won't fall behind any others!

17:20.680 --> 17:22.230
Right, Tsubasa?

17:22.230 --> 17:24.890
Uh? Oh, yes.

17:24.890 --> 17:27.850
But Misugi really is too strong.

17:28.600 --> 17:29.610
Tsubasa!

17:29.610 --> 17:31.610
What happened, Tsubasa? Even you're like this?

17:31.610 --> 17:32.610
Tsubasa...

17:34.240 --> 17:36.530
<i>He has more technical skill than me.</i>

17:38.640 --> 17:39.940
<i>He does the job of directing his team</i>

17:39.940 --> 17:43.880
<i>as a captain better than I can,</i>

17:43.880 --> 17:48.420
<i>with the added handicap of a heart disease.</i>

17:49.050 --> 17:53.420
<i>There's no way I can win.</i>

17:54.280 --> 17:57.380
Um, what is it you wanted to talk about, captain?

18:02.690 --> 18:03.970
Huh?

18:04.980 --> 18:08.420
Why did you tell Tsubasa about my heart condition?!

18:10.900 --> 18:17.020
Because of you, our battle was cut short, twice!

18:18.740 --> 18:21.910
You happened to find out about my condition by mistake,

18:21.910 --> 18:24.910
and have taken care of me since then.

18:25.410 --> 18:29.240
But this match is between Tsubasa and me.

18:29.240 --> 18:31.170
You had no right to involve yourself as you did.

18:33.880 --> 18:36.660
I am very sorry, captain.

18:45.060 --> 18:47.210
What happened, boss?

18:47.210 --> 18:50.370
We'll turn the tables around in the second half!

18:50.370 --> 18:51.100
It's not that.

18:51.840 --> 18:57.110
It's... if Nankatsu wins, Tsubasa will be going to Brazil.

18:58.060 --> 19:01.680
If Tsubasa will stay in Japan otherwise,

19:01.680 --> 19:04.660
then maybe it's okay if he loses here.

19:04.660 --> 19:05.910
Eh?!

19:06.590 --> 19:08.910
<i>The second half starts now!</i>

19:08.910 --> 19:12.210
<i>This was the first time Tsubasa had</i>

19:12.210 --> 19:14.130
<i>gone to the field in such a mood.</i>

19:14.130 --> 19:16.130
<i>Despite being usually filled with confidence and</i>

19:16.130 --> 19:18.300
<i>calling the ball his friend,</i>

19:18.300 --> 19:21.350
<i>he now stands on the field,</i>

19:21.350 --> 19:23.590
<i>filled with unease.</i>

19:23.590 --> 19:27.600
His mood has changed from the first half.

19:27.600 --> 19:30.100
Let's get back in the mood, Tsubasa!

19:30.100 --> 19:32.600
<i>The ball is passed to Tsubasa!</i>

19:35.280 --> 19:38.140
<i>What's this? Tsubasa makes a mistake trapping the ball!</i>

19:38.140 --> 19:38.610
That's mine now!

19:39.550 --> 19:40.820
What's happened, Tsubasa!?

19:40.820 --> 19:43.030
Our showdown has just started!

19:43.500 --> 19:44.910
Misugi!

19:44.910 --> 19:46.450
Move to attack!

19:46.450 --> 19:47.910
Everbody, fall back!

19:47.910 --> 19:51.000
We have to defend this at all costs.

19:53.210 --> 19:54.460
All right! It's mine now!

19:55.890 --> 19:57.450
<i>Misaki comes through!</i>

19:57.450 --> 19:59.960
<i>Nankatsu is saved by mere inches!</i>

19:59.960 --> 20:04.810
<i>As I thought, Misaki is the key in this match.</i>

20:04.810 --> 20:10.560
<i>But the real ace of Nankatsu is you, Tsubasa.</i>

20:10.560 --> 20:13.320
<i>Don't let it end here, please.</i>

20:13.320 --> 20:17.570
<i>Put everything into it and challenge me, Tsubasa!</i>

20:20.100 --> 20:21.240
It's raining!

20:22.180 --> 20:23.990
Tsubasa, I'm counting on you!

20:26.350 --> 20:27.870
Tsubasa, it's on!

20:28.560 --> 20:29.700
Misugi!

20:31.370 --> 20:32.540
Tsubasa!

20:34.660 --> 20:37.790
<i>Tsubasa makes a pass to Misaki!</i>

20:37.790 --> 20:40.250
We're counting on you, Nankatsu's Golden Duo!

20:40.940 --> 20:42.340
Tsubasa—

20:42.340 --> 20:43.680
<i>What is happening?</i>

20:43.680 --> 20:45.840
<i>Tsubasa is not keeping up with Misaki!</i>

20:46.300 --> 20:48.850
<i>I won't be able to match Misugi.</i>

20:49.920 --> 20:50.890
Tsubasa.

20:51.680 --> 20:53.980
<i>Misugi has stolen the ball!</i>

20:54.890 --> 20:56.810
<i>What's with you, Tsubasa?</i>

20:56.810 --> 20:59.730
<i>Have you lost the will to fight?</i>

21:01.680 --> 21:03.240
<i>I'm no match for him.</i>

21:03.240 --> 21:06.240
<i>I beg of you, Tsubasa, come towards me.</i>

21:06.240 --> 21:08.530
<i>Stop me!</i>

21:09.280 --> 21:10.450
<i>No match at all.</i>

21:11.180 --> 21:14.750
<i>Ah! Misugi has passed through Tsubasa!</i>

21:17.880 --> 21:19.140
<i>It's over.</i>

21:20.250 --> 21:23.300
Tsubasa!

21:24.140 --> 21:27.980
<i>I can't. I can't beat him.</i>

21:30.050 --> 21:33.810
<i>Sanada scores the goal! It's 3-1!</i>

21:33.810 --> 21:36.410
<i>A 2 goal lead at last!</i>

21:36.410 --> 21:39.060
I really didn't think it would become like this.

21:39.620 --> 21:43.320
<i>Has Tsubasa's poor condition caused a chain effect?</i>

21:43.680 --> 21:46.700
<i>Nankatsu's players' movements have become slow as well.</i>

21:46.700 --> 21:49.980
<i>Have they lost their stamina in the first half?</i>

21:49.980 --> 21:52.180
This is the power of Nankatsu!

21:52.950 --> 21:56.180
This is the power of Nankatsu, who can't

21:56.180 --> 21:58.920
hold a candle to us, Musashi FC.

21:58.920 --> 22:02.450
Everyone, this is our match now.

22:02.450 --> 22:05.590
Don't hold back. Crush Nankatsu!

22:05.590 --> 22:07.470
Yeah!

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.830 --> 22:44.710
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.710 --> 22:50.720
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.720
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.720 --> 22:56.720
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.720 --> 23:02.190
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.720 --> 23:02.190
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:08.320
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.150 --> 23:08.320
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.030
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.030
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.030 --> 23:21.080
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.080 --> 23:26.090
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.380 --> 23:33.260
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.380 --> 23:33.260
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.260 --> 23:39.140
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:46.020
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.140 --> 23:46.020
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.110 --> 24:00.720
COMING UP, EPISODE 21:
THE ACE OF GLASS
